const PROMPT = "You classify customer requests for a service company.
Return JSON with exactly these fields:
- type: one of "Complaint", "General Enquiry", "Service Request"
- urgency: one of "low", "medium", "high"
- confidence: a number from 0 to 1
- reason: one short sentence

Definitions:
- Complaint: the customer is unhappy about something that went wrong.
- General Enquiry: the customer asks for information. Nothing needs to be done on their account.
- Service Request: the customer asks us to do or change something on their account.
Urgency rules:
- high: fraud or money taken without permission, a lost or stolen card, a complete loss of service or account access, or the customer says they need action immediately or today.
- medium: a problem that has gone on for days, happened more than once, or was not fixed after earlier contact, but the customer can still use the service. Also requests tied to a deadline or an upcoming trip.
- low: general questions, routine changes, and minor annoyances.
Do not use high for a bad experience alone. Anger or disappointment does not make a request high.
Confidence rules:
- Use 0.9 or higher only when the request clearly fits exactly one type.
- If the message is vague, has no clear request, or could fit more than one type, use a confidence below 0.6.

Request: {text}
";
const REPLY_PROMPT = "You write short customer replies for an operations team.
Write one reply of at most 70 words to the customer request below.
Rules:
- Polite, plain language. Start with "Hi," and end with "Customer Care Team".
- What the reply must do: {instruction}
- Do not invent facts, names, prices or timeframes that are not in these instructions or the FAQ.

Customer request: {text}
{extra}";
const ENQUIRY_PROMPT = "You answer customer enquiries for a service company.
Customer enquiry: {text}

FAQ:
{faq}

Return JSON with exactly these fields:
- subtopic: 2 to 4 words naming what the enquiry is about, for example "student discount", "billing statements", "opening hours"
- reply: one customer reply of at most 70 words. Polite, plain language. Start with "Hi," and end with "Customer Care Team". Answer using only the FAQ above. If the FAQ does not cover the question, say a team member will confirm the answer by email. Do not invent facts, names, prices or timeframes.";
const SERVICE_PROMPT = "You triage service requests for a service company's operations team.
Customer request: {text}

Return JSON with exactly these fields:
- summary: one sentence stating what the customer wants done, including every specific detail they gave (for example a new address or a date). Add no details they did not give.
- department: exactly one of: Billing, Account Services, Technical Support, Plan Changes, Service Desk. Billing is for payments, invoices and refunds. Account Services is for changing personal or account details. Technical Support is for faults and setup help. Plan Changes is for upgrading, downgrading or cancelling a plan. Service Desk is for anything else.
- reply: one customer reply of at most 70 words. Polite, plain language. Start with "Hi," and end with "Customer Care Team". Confirm you received the request, restate what they asked for using only their own words, say it has been passed to the department you chose, and say it will be actioned within 1 business day. Do not invent facts, names, prices or timeframes.";
const DEPARTMENTS = ["Billing", "Account Services", "Technical Support", "Plan Changes", "Service Desk"];
const INSTR = {"Complaint": "Apologise, show you understand the specific problem, confirm you received the complaint, and say it has been passed to a senior member of the team who will follow up. Do not give a timeframe.", "General Enquiry": "Answer using only the FAQ below. If the FAQ does not cover the question, say a team member will confirm the answer by email.", "Service Request": "Confirm you received the request, restate what they asked for using only their own words (add no details they did not give), and say it will be actioned within 1 business day.", "Reminder": "Apologise for the wait, say the case is still open and a senior member of the team is following it up, and say they will hear from the team again soon. Do not give a timeframe.", "Urgent Escalation": "Acknowledge the urgency, say the case has been escalated to a priority team, and say someone will contact them within 2 hours."};
const FAQ = "SAMPLE FAQ (made up for this demo; not real company information)
- Opening hours: Monday to Friday 8am to 6pm, Saturday 9am to 1pm. Closed on public holidays, but online help is available 24/7.
- Student discount: Students get 10% off any plan with a valid student ID.
- Statements: Log in, open Documents, choose Statements and select the last 12 months to download.
- Opening an account: You need photo ID and proof of address, such as a utility bill or bank statement.
- Card payments: Paying by credit card has a 1.5% fee. Bank transfer and direct debit are free.
- Plans: Basic includes standard support. Premium adds priority support and a higher monthly allowance.
- International callers: Call +61 3 5550 0100 (sample number).
- Late payment: Bills are due 14 days after the statement date. A late fee of $10 applies after that.
- Changing plans: You can change plan at any time from your account. The new plan starts on your next billing date.
- Cancelling: Cancel any time from your account or by phone. There are no exit fees on month-to-month plans.
- Direct debit: Set up direct debit in your account under Payments. It takes effect from the next bill.
- Updating details: Change your address, phone number or email in your account under Profile.
- Lost or stolen card: Call the 24/7 line straight away so the card can be blocked. A replacement arrives in 5 business days.
- Refunds: Refunds for billing errors are returned to the original payment method within 7 business days.
- Making a complaint: You can complain by phone, email or online. We acknowledge every complaint on the day we receive it.
- Online account: Register with your account number and email. A reset link is sent if you forget your password.
- Service outages: Check the status page for known outages. We post updates every hour until service is restored.
";
const b = $input.first().json.body || $input.first().json;
const request = String(b.request || '').trim();
if (!request) { throw new Error('No request text received'); }
const prompt = PROMPT.replace('{text}', () => request);
const ov = b.reminder_minutes_override;
return [{ json: {
